## Loss of LATS kinases results in carcinoma-like murine tumours
Postnatal analysis of $H e s x\mathcal{1}^{C r e/+};L a t s\mathcal{1}^{\mathcal{H}//\mathcal{H}}$ pituitaries revealed that by P56, despite developing normally during the embryonic period, all glands examined exhibited lesions of abnormal morphology consisting of overgrowths, densely packed nuclei and loss of normal acinar architecture $(n=15)$ . To minimise the likely redundancy by LATS2 seen at embryonic stages, we generated Lats1 mutants additionally haploinsufficient for Lats2 $(H e s x\mathcal{I}^{C r e/+};L a t s\mathcal{I}^{{f l/f l}};L a t s2^{{f l/+}})$ . These pituitaries also developed identifiable lesions accumulating YAP and TAZ (Figure 3—figure supplement 1A), which were observed at earlier time points $(\mathsf{P21}\mathsf{n}=4)$ ), the earliest being 10 days, indicating increased severity. The number of lesions observed per animal was similar between the two models at P56 (3–8 per animal). Deletion of Lats2 alone $(H e s x\mathcal{1}^{C r e/+};L a t s2^{f l/f t})_{.}$ , which is barely expressed in the wild type pituitary, did not result in any defects (Figure 3—figure supplement 1B). We focused on the $H e s x1^{C r e/+}$ ; Lats1fl/fl;Lats2fl/+ double mutants for further analyses.
Histological examination of $H e s x1^{C r e/+};L a t s1^{{f i}/{f t}};L a t s2^{{f l}/{f}+}$ pituitaries confirmed the abnormal lesions were tumours, characterised by frequent mitoses, focal necrosis, and a focal squamous differentiation, as well as the occasional presence of cysts (Figure 3A). These lesions were identical to those in $H e s x\mathcal{1}^{C r e/+};L a t s\mathcal{1}^{{\sf f l/f}{\sf I}}$ pituitaries (not shown). These tumours accumulated YAP/TAZ and upregulated expression of targets Cyr61 and Ctgf (Figure 3B), confirming the validity of the genetic manipulation (Figure 3B). Tumours were also frequently observed in the anterior and intermediate lobe (Figure 3—figure supplement 1C). Analysis of proliferation by Ki-67 immunostaining revealed an elevated mitotic index of $7-28\%$ in tumours (mean 15.46, SEM $\pm2.74\$ ), compared to $2.97\%$ (SEM $\pm1.2)$ mean in control pituitaries not carrying the Lats1 deletion (Figure 3C).
In keeping with the morphological evidence of epithelial differentiation (Figure 3A), the tumours were positive for cytokeratins using AE1/AE3 (multiple keratin cocktail) (Figure 3—figure supplement 1E). Furthermore, the tumours showed focal morphological evidence of squamous differentiation and showed positive nuclear p63 staining, frequently expressed in squamous carcinomas
